WEBVTT

00:19:27.447 --> 00:19:31.706
And to say, no, we've got
something wrong here,

00:19:31.730 --> 00:19:34.709
that the unit of change
is the neighborhood -- talk about that.

00:19:34.733 --> 00:19:37.747
DB: I do think that's right.
We've taken individualism too far.

00:19:37.771 --> 00:19:40.550
We imagine human creatures
are these individual,

00:19:40.574 --> 00:19:43.799
utility-maximizing creatures
motivated by money, status and power.

00:19:43.823 --> 00:19:46.596
And these weavers are not motivated
by any of those things.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:49.163
They want to live by
the real things that motivate us:

00:19:49.187 --> 00:19:52.593
to be in right relation with each other
and to serve some ultimate good.

00:19:52.617 --> 00:19:54.542
And so, that's philosophically the case.

00:19:54.566 --> 00:19:58.121
In the social science term, just take,
for example, the work of Raj Chetty,

00:19:58.145 --> 00:20:01.208
who is a great economist
who is dominating the world these days.